1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,300
MissionForge

2
00:00:01,340 --> 00:00:05,210
A party game where your team designs
a space mission, then flies it.

3
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:06,708
Design a space mission.
Every choice costs something.

4
00:00:06,748 --> 00:00:08,262
Mass, power, budget, instruments,
orbit, communications

5
00:00:08,302 --> 00:00:10,494
Contract C1 Earth Watch:
a 150 kg imaging satellite

6
00:00:10,534 --> 00:00:12,710
to a 550 km Sun-synchronous orbit (97.6°),
on 90 M game-dollars, in 180 days.

7
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:13,750
One big screen hosts the mission

8
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:15,710
The Unity host runs on a laptop
or TV; phones are the controllers.

9
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:17,360
Join with a 4-letter
room code or the QR code

10
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,710
No app, no account, no chat. 1
to 10 players, plus an audience.

11
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:21,783
Type a call sign and you are in the crew

12
00:00:21,823 --> 00:00:25,710
The phone is the controller: role
console, part cards, votes and minigames.

13
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:27,159
Each phone becomes a mission-control console

14
00:00:27,199 --> 00:00:29,124
10 roles, from FLIGHT and BOOSTER
to EECOM, INCO and PAYLOAD.

15
00:00:29,164 --> 00:00:30,710
With fewer players, roles
merge automatically.

16
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:33,278
22 part votes build the
rocket and the satellite

17
00:00:33,318 --> 00:00:35,948
The dashboard shows delta-v,
thrust-to-weight, cost,

18
00:00:35,988 --> 00:00:38,710
schedule, power and data
before the team commits.

19
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:41,186
Every option shows its
numbers and its drawbacks

20
00:00:41,226 --> 00:00:43,559
Thrust, Isp, mass, cost
and a real-world twin.

21
00:00:43,599 --> 00:00:45,880
A card warns when an option is over budget.

22
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,210
There is no perfect build

23
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:48,948
“If chosen” shows what each option changes

24
00:00:48,988 --> 00:00:52,052
Small fairing: +$2.0 M. Standard fairing:
+$5.0 M and a structures concern.

25
00:00:52,092 --> 00:00:53,210
(Costs are game-dollars.)

26
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:55,062
The crew votes, and the build updates

27
00:00:55,102 --> 00:00:58,617
Live tallies, then the phone’s
readiness dashboard after each decision:

28
00:00:58,657 --> 00:01:01,210
delta-v, thrust-to-weight,
budget, success chance.

29
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:02,250
Compare two options side by side

30
00:01:02,290 --> 00:01:03,710
Also: exploded view, scale
reference and stability markers.

31
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:06,710
The vehicle is assembled live in 3D

32
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:08,805
Every console calls GO or NO-GO

33
00:01:08,845 --> 00:01:13,710
As in a real readiness review, a NO-GO
stops the count for a discussion.

34
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:15,964
Consoles call out problems in flight

35
00:01:16,004 --> 00:01:19,210
Max Q is coming: STRUCT calls the
throttle-down for a Good Call.

36
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:20,262
Max Q Throttle Bucket

37
00:01:20,302 --> 00:01:23,418
Keep dynamic pressure inside the
band to protect the structure.

38
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:24,710
32 minigames on the phone

39
00:01:24,750 --> 00:01:25,816
Solar Wing Deploy

40
00:01:25,856 --> 00:01:28,710
Turn the wings to the Sun
to stay power-positive.

41
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:29,996
Ground Station Pass

42
00:01:30,036 --> 00:01:32,710
Steer the antenna, lock
on and downlink the data.

43
00:01:32,750 --> 00:01:33,821
Science Capture

44
00:01:33,861 --> 00:01:36,710
Point the instrument you chose.
Clouds block optical shots.

45
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:39,005
The debrief explains the result

46
00:01:39,045 --> 00:01:44,710
Score breakdown, awards, and the facts
met along the way, each with its source.

47
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:46,028
Six languages. Large text. High contrast.

48
00:01:46,068 --> 00:01:48,762
English, Arabic (right to left),
Spanish, French, Portuguese, Hindi.

49
00:01:48,802 --> 00:01:50,691
200% text, reduced motion,
relaxed and one-button minigames.

50
00:01:50,731 --> 00:01:52,210
Left: Arabic. Right:
200% text, high contrast.

51
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:54,029
MissionForge
Design it. Launch it. Learn why it worked.

52
00:01:54,069 --> 00:01:55,484
Team Winton · NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026

53
00:01:55,524 --> 00:01:58,097
Built with AI coding agents. Key art
and briefing film are AI-generated.

54
00:01:58,137 --> 00:01:59,460
Not affiliated with or endorsed by NASA.
